# The pinned serving config for allenai/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct on one RTX 5090: the shape the routing-histogram
# experiment (experiments/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct/routing_histogram_rtx5090) serves, and the config its golden's
# serving twins are traced from (`emmy trace --serving-twins --serving-config`). Syntax rules: see gemma-4-12b-it.env.
#
# One sequence at a time (--max-num-seqs 1): decode rides the 16-row twins, prefill chunks of up to 512 tokens ride
# the any-width programs. The 0.75 memory fraction leaves room for a desktop on the card. Strict evidence makes a boot
# whose golden lacks a measured row fail at compile time instead of deploying a prior pick: without its golden, the
# prior's pick for the routed-expert program recomputes the gate/up projection for every output of the down
# projection and runs for seconds per launch, which looks like a hang in vLLM's profile run.
SERVE_MODEL=allenai/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct
SERVE_REVISION=b89a7c4bc24fb9e55ce2543c9458ce0ca5c4650e
SERVE_GOLDEN_FILE=recipes/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct/golden/rtx5090_sm120.json
SERVE_MAX_MODEL_LEN=4096
SERVE_MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=512
SERVE_PREFILL_CAPACITY=512
SERVE_PREFILL_BUCKET=0
SERVE_DECODE_BUCKET=16
SERVE_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.75
SERVE_GPU="NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090"
SERVE_EXTRA_ARGS="--dtype float16 --max-num-seqs 1 --no-enable-prefix-caching"
SERVE_CAPTURE_SIZES="[1]"
SERVE_M1_TIER=0
SERVE_ENV="EMMY_STRICT_EVIDENCE=1"
